  <tr>
    <td style="width: 33%;"><img src="https://images.code.org/ec08ed532bb06832510a6cccffd4bb92-image-1784158994785.42.49 PM.png" alt="A code snippet that reads custom.turn_right(aria)" style="width: 100%;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: left; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; font-size:14pt;">
      In this option, the function is being <i>called</i>, not defined.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 33%;"><img src="https://images.code.org/d5ec19d31f86a4401f169d6e396f19c3-image-1784158994772.42.21 PM.png" alt="A code snippet that is missing a color after def turn_right(painter) " style="width: 100%;"></td>
    <td style="text-align: left; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; font-size:14pt;">
      In this option, the colon <code>:</code> is left off the header which will result in an error.
